1
00:09:06,666 --> 00:09:12,666
The world was watching in 1972 as 11 Israeli athletes were murdered at the
Munich Olympics. This is the story of what happened next.

2
00:18:13,333 --> 00:18:19,333
Munich is a drama, action, history film directed by Steven Spielberg.

3
00:27:20,000 --> 00:27:26,000
During the 1972 Olympic Games in Munich, eleven Israeli athletes are taken hostage and
murdered by a Palestinian terrorist group known as Black September.

4
00:36:26,666 --> 00:36:32,666
In retaliation, the Israeli government recruits a group of Mossad agents to
track down and execute those responsible for the attack.

5
00:45:33,333 --> 00:45:39,333
Avner, played by Eric Bana.

6
00:54:40,000 --> 00:54:46,000
Steve, played by Daniel Craig.

7
01:03:46,666 --> 01:03:52,666
Carl, played by Ciarán Hinds.

8
01:12:53,333 --> 01:12:59,333
Robert, played by Mathieu Kassovitz.

9
01:22:00,000 --> 01:22:06,000
Hans, played by Hanns Zischler.

10
01:31:06,666 --> 01:31:12,666
Daphna, played by Ayelet Zurer.

11
01:40:13,333 --> 01:40:19,333
Munich is a 2005 epic historical drama film produced and directed by
Steven Spielberg, co-written by Tony Kushner and Eric Roth.

12
01:49:20,000 --> 01:49:26,000
It is based on the 1984 book Vengeance by George Jonas, an account of
Mossad assassinations following the Munich massacre.

13
01:58:26,666 --> 01:58:32,666
Munich was released by Universal Pictures in the United States and Canada and internationally by DreamWorks Pictures on December 23, 2005,
and received five Oscar nominations: Best Picture, Best Director, Best Adapted Screenplay, Best Editing, and Best Score.

14
02:07:33,333 --> 02:07:39,333
The film made $131 million worldwide but just $47 million in the United States,
making it one of Spielberg's lowest-grossing films domestically.

15
02:16:40,000 --> 02:16:46,000
In 2017, the film was named the 16th "Best Film of the
21st Century So Far" by The New York Times.

16
02:25:46,666 --> 02:25:52,666
The film explores themes of hotel room, israel,
mossad, assassination, paris, france.

17
02:34:53,333 --> 02:34:59,333
The tone is emotional and intense.
